# Helpy Cursor Rules

## Critical Patterns - DO NOT MODIFY

### Bottom Sheets - MUST BE ABOVE BOTTOM NAV

**RULE: Every bottom sheet/modal MUST use `createPortal` to render to `document.body`.**

This ensures bottom sheets ALWAYS appear above the bottom navigation bar, regardless of any CSS stacking contexts.

#### Option 1: Use the BottomSheet Component (Preferred)

```tsx
import BottomSheet from '@/components/ui/BottomSheet';

<BottomSheet isOpen={isOpen} onClose={() => setIsOpen(false)}>
  <BottomSheet.Header>
    <h2 className="text-title text-foreground">Title</h2>
  </BottomSheet.Header>
  <BottomSheet.Body>
    <p>Content</p>
  </BottomSheet.Body>
  <BottomSheet.Footer>
    <button>Action</button>
  </BottomSheet.Footer>
</BottomSheet>
```

#### Option 2: Manual createPortal (for custom modals)

```tsx
import { createPortal } from 'react-dom';

{isOpen && createPortal(
  <div className="fixed inset-0 bg-black/30 backdrop-blur-sm z-[60] flex items-end justify-center bottom-sheet-backdrop">
    {/* Safe area cover */}
    <div className="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 bg-card" style={{ height: 'env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 34px)' }} />
    <div className="bg-card w-full max-w-lg rounded-t-2xl overflow-hidden bottom-sheet-content" style={{ marginBottom: 'env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 34px)' }}>
      {/* Content */}
    </div>
  </div>
, document.body)}
```

#### Why This Matters

- CSS `animation` and `opacity` properties create stacking contexts
- Elements inside a stacking context cannot escape it with z-index
- The Layout component wraps page content, creating potential stacking issues
- `createPortal` renders directly to `document.body`, bypassing all stacking contexts

#### Z-Index Hierarchy

| Element | Z-Index |
|---------|---------|
| Bottom Navigation | `z-10` |
| Sticky Headers | `z-20` |
| Dropdowns | `z-50` |
| **Bottom Sheets/Modals** | `z-[60]` + `createPortal` |
| `.bottom-sheet-backdrop` CSS | `z-index: 9999 !important` |

**NEVER create a bottom sheet without `createPortal` or the `BottomSheet` component!**

---

### Meals.tsx Structure

The Meals page MUST use the exact same structure as ToDo and Expenses:

```tsx
<div className="min-h-screen bg-background pb-40">
  <div className="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 page-content">
    <header className="sticky top-0 z-20 bg-background -mx-4 px-4 sm:-mx-6 sm:px-6 ...">
```

Key rules:
1. Header INSIDE the `page-content` wrapper (not outside)
2. Header uses `-mx-4 px-4 sm:-mx-6 sm:px-6` to extend edge-to-edge
3. Use `useEffect` with MULTIPLE TIMED ATTEMPTS (0ms, 50ms, 150ms, 300ms) for auto-scroll
4. NO scroll-pending/scroll-ready classes

See `docs/MEALS_SCROLL_FIX.md` for details.

---

## Code Style

- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Follow existing component patterns
- Keep translations in the `t` object
- Use `useScrollHeader` hook for sticky header animations
- Use `useScrollLock` when modals are open
